  "reason": "The current best (config_039, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. The dominant factor identified so far is the RNA encoder (scvi_n200 vs scgpt gives ~20% gain), while fusion (weighted vs concat) shows only a ~0.4% difference. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the transformer aggregation is truly necessary or whether a simpler avgpool aggregation performs comparably with the strong scvi_n200 encoder. Config_021 changes exactly one variable from the best (transformer → avgpool, keeping weighted fusion), directly testing whether aggregation architecture matters. This is the best use of experiment 6 because: (1) it is a clean single-variable ablation of the current best, (2) if avgpool matches transformer, it confirms the model is not aggregation-limited and remaining budget can focus on other axes (e.g., image encoder or profile setting); if it falls short, it confirms transformer is essential and we should exploit that. With only 4 experiments left, resolving this uncertainty efficiently is critical."
